ate solution for harmonious family dinners might hinge on individual tastes and experiences. Some families have found eMeals’ recipes to be more tailored towards adult ‘foodies’ rather than children, potentially affecting family approval rates.\n\nIn conclusion, while eMeals offers numerous benefits such as diverse meal plans, seamless grocery integration, and time-saving strategies, its suitability for your family will largely depend on your family members’ taste preferences and your willingness to try new recipes. It might not be the perfect solution for everyone, but for many, it could just be the meal planning hack they’ve been waiting for.\n\n## Summary\n\nTo wrap up, eMeals is a comprehensive meal planning service that aims to simplify the meal planning process for busy families. It offers a variety of meal plans, a user-friendly app, and seamless integration with grocery delivery services. It also provides a wide selection of recipes and the ability to customize your meal plans and shopping lists.\n\nHowever, as with any service, it’s not without its flaws. Some users have reported issues with flavor and inaccurate cooking times, and there have been concerns about the service’s suitability for families with children or picky eaters. Despite these issues, many users find the convenience and variety offered by eMeals to be a valuable addition to their meal planning routine.\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### How much does eMeals cost?\n\neMeals costs $4.99 per month with a 12-month commitment or $35.99 for a 3-month option, making it an affordable choice for meal planning.\n\n### Can I customize my meal plans on eMeals?\n\nAbsolutely! eMeals gives you the flexibility to customize your meal plans by mixing and matching from different options and excluding any meals you don’t want. Enjoy creating a personalized experience!\n\n### Can I use eMeals on multiple devices?\n\nYes, you can use eMeals on multiple devices, but some users have experienced problems with the app’s sync functionality when switching between devices. Be mindful of potential sync issues.\n\n### What grocery delivery services does eMeals integrate with?\n\neMeals integrates with popular grocery delivery services like Walmart, Instacart, Amazon, Kroger, and Shipt. This makes it convenient for you to choose the one that works best for you.\n\n### Can I try eMeals before committing to a subscription?\n\nYes, you can try eMeals before committing to a subscription with a 14-day trial to explore the service.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n50% Off | eMeals Meal Plans (https://try.emeals.com/limited-time/)\nciteturn94search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; \n\n## Take Care of Your To-Do List\n\nAs you select your recipes for the week, we'll automatically create an editable shopping list with all the ingredients.\n\n## New Dinner Ideas Every Week\n\nSimple, healthy meals to fit your busy lifestyle.\n\nQuick & Healthy\n\nSimple, healthy meals to fit your busy lifestyle.\n\n30 Minute\n\nEnjoy quick-and-easy mainstream dinners. \n\nBudget Friendly\n\nFast, affordable dinners your family will love.\n\n\nOnce your shopping list is complete, easily send it to your local grocery store for curbside pickup or delivery. \n\nSelect your meal plan (with access to all 15 plans), and we'll send over seven new recipes  every Wednesday.\n\nChoose Weekly Meals\n\nReview Shopping List\n\nSend List to the Store\n\n\n#### Weekly Variety with Easy Shopping\n\nEasy meals even the pickiest eaters will love.\n\nQUICK AND HEALTHY\n\nFajita Ground Beef Skillet\n\n## New Dinner Ideas Every Week\n\nSimple, healthy meals to fit your busy lifestyle.\n\nKETO\n\n20-Minute Steak Strips\n\nCheddar Mashed Cauliflower and Garlic Zucchini\n\nKID FRIENDLY\n\nBrown Sugar-Baked Chicken\n\n# We miss you. Come back and save 50%!\n\nGet 1 Year of eMeals for ~~$59.99~~ $29.99\n\nSave 50% Off Today >\n\n\n#### New Weekly Meal Inspiration\n\nFull Access to 15 Meal Plans\n\nCustomizable Shopping List\n\n#### Convenient Online Grocery Options\n\nBonus Collections & Occasions Plans\n\n## Skip the Store with eMeals and Walmart\n\nLimited Time Offer: Save 50% >Claim 50% Off!\n\n#### Easy Shopping List Generator\n\n#### Save Time by Skipping the Grocery Line\n\n#### Healthy Meal Plans That Don't Break the Bank\n\n#### Save $10 on Your First Walmart Order\n\nGet 1 Year of eMeals for ~~$59.99~~ $29.99\n\nLimited Time Offer: Save 50% >\n\n\nUse code Comeback50 to claim your personal offer. \n\nUse code ComeBack50 to claim your personal offer.\n\nTry Free for 14 Days\n\nClaim Your 50% Off\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow much does Plan to Eat cost? (https://learn.plantoeat.com/help/how-much-does-plan-to-eat-cost)\nciteturn94search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Crawled: last month; \n\nHow can we help?\n\nFind answers to your Plan to Eat questions including getting started, features, and common issues.\n\nHow much does Plan to Eat cost?\n\nGetting Started\n\n# How much does Plan to Eat cost?\n\nWe have two subscription options: annual and monthly\n\nLast updated on 22 Oct, 2025\n\nWe offer two subscriptions, $49 a year or $5.95 a month.\n\nOur yearly plan is our best value, and is only $4.08 a month compared to our monthly plan.\n\nPurchasing through the Apple App Store is $54.99 because Apple charges us a fee for payments made through the app. You can always subscribe online and save $5 on your annual subscription. \n\n  Prices reflect cost in US Dollars. If you are purchasing Plan to Eat with a credit card issued outside of the US, exchange rates will apply and you will be charged based on local currency amounts. \n\n### Why isn't there a free plan?\n\nYou may have heard the saying if you’re not paying for the product, then you are the product. We don’t believe in making money by selling your data to the highest bidder, but we still need funds to create the best meal-planning software available.\n\nWhen you pay us a monthly or annual subscription, you’re contributing to a fully customer-funded business, which allows us to be customer-focused and avoid being sleazy data salespeople.\n\nRead more about our stance on not selling your data.\n\nAnd if you don’t love Plan to Eat, you can get a prompt and courteous refund within the first 60 days - just email us with your refund request. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMeal Planner, Recipe Organizer, and Automatic Grocery Lists - Plan to Eat (https://www.plantoeat.com/)\nciteturn94search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; \n\nSmart Meal Planning\n\n### No More Messy Lists\n\nBuy everything you need from a clear, aisle-by-aisle list.\n\nStreamlined Shopping\n\nTry Plan To Eat\n\nStart for free!\n\nNo card info, no hassle. Just a simpler week.\nOnly $5.95/mo or $49/year if you choose to subscribe.\n\nGet Started Today\n\n(opens in a new tab)(opens in a new tab)\n\n★★★★★ 4.8 on the App Store · 4.7 on Google Play\n\nAn App for Do-ers\n\n## You’re in control. Add your recipes, move meals around anytime, and plan in a way that works for you.\n\nImage: Image\n\nThis tool has transformed what used to be a burden into a simple, quick and easy task I can tackle in less than 30 minutes on the weekend – including building my online grocery order for the week’s pick-up! Now that my kids are teenagers, time is even more precious and Plan to Eat has allowed me to capture just a bit of that back each week. I can’t imagine trying to plan, shop, and cook meals for my family without it!\n\nThe Numbers\n\n## Make a life-changing difference.\n\n47.5%\n\n### Reduction in time spent planning and grocery shopping.\n\nThe average time of our 2,568 survey respondents spent planning and grocery shopping was reduced from 140 to 73 minutes per week.\n\n23%\n\n### Reduction in food costs.\n\nThe average food cost of the 2,568 customers surveyed, per person in the household per month was reduced from $199 to $152.\n\n73%\n\n### Increase in consumption of \"healthier foods.\"\n\n“Plan to Eat simplifies the process of locating and planning healthy recipes that my family will enjoy.”\n\n46%\n\n### Ate more meals together at home.\n\nThe average number of dinners eaten together at home per week increased from 3.6 to 5.6.\n\n86%\n\n### Reported a decrease in anxiety about meals.\n\n“A little planning upfront saves a ton of frustration during the week. Especially with kids—it’s nice to know what’s for dinner every day.”\n\nTry Plan To Eat\n\nMake meal planning finally stick!\n\nYour recipes, your schedule, your plan. \nOnly $5.95/mo or $49/year if you choose to subscribe.\n\nGet Started Today\n\n(opens in a new tab)(opens in a new tab)\n\n★★★★★ 4.8 on the App Store · 4.7 on Google Play\n\n* * *\n\nImage: Image\n\nPlan to Eat is a powerful tool to make meal planning as painless as possible using your family’s favorite recipes. One of my favorite things to do is plan a meal on the fly when I see a bargain while shopping. Plan To Eat lives on the home screen of my phone – prime real estate!\n\nImage: Image\n\nSusan Cramer\n\nOwner, Motivated Moms\n\nThe Bottom Line\n\n## Plan to Eat brings order to chaos.\n\nWith Plan to Eat, your bookmarked recipes, the kitchen whiteboard, and a scribbled shopping list are transformed into a single, meal planning system you can trust.\n\n### Recipe Clipper\n\nOur Recipe Clipper allows you to gather all your recipes together in your digital recipe book and organize them how you like.\n\n### Planning Calendar\n\nThe meal planning calendar lets you plan ahead for any length of time, save meal plans to reuse in the future and add notes to remind yourself of the other events and obligations in your life.\n\n### Automated Shopping List\n\nBut the very best part of Plan to Eat is the automated shopping list. When you add recipes to your calendar, the shopping list will automatically populate an organized list of ingredients you need to buy.\n\nYou can add to and refine this list as much as you want, so you buy all the ingredients for your recipes, and any other household items you also need.\n\nAchieve meal planning success with Plan to Eat.\n\nStart your trial, for free, for 14 days!\n\nNo payment information required, so there’s nothing to cancel if you decide we’re not right for you. And one account gets you (and your family) access on all your devices. You can subscribe at the end of your free trial for $5.95 a month or $49 per year (4 months free).\n\nThe Origin Story\n\n## Plan to Eat is the tool we wished for.\n\nWith a growing family, Lisa Bounds wanted to eat out less and cook at home more. She started meal planning with pen and paper, and a stack of recipe books. It helped her family eat at home more and save money on food, but meal planning was time-consuming.\n\nHer husband, Clint, tried to find a digital solution to make meal planning easier, but in the early 2000s, nothing existed. So Clint, a designer and web developer, set out to create a digital meal-planning program for his wife.\n\nIn 2008, Lisa’s pen-and-paper process was transformed into a website, and the first iteration of Plan to Eat was born. Clint quit his full-time job to work exclusively on Plan to Eat and since then, the program has helped thousands of meal planners simplify their planning process.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow do I get a refund? (https://learn.plantoeat.com/help/refunds-16)\nciteturn94search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\nHow do I get a refund?\n\n# How do I get a refund?\n\nRefunds and cancellations can be requested for monthly or yearly purchases.\n\nLast updated on 23 Mar, 2026\n\n### Refunds for purchases made on our website:\n\nWe have a 60-day 'no questions asked' refund policy for annual subscriptions purchased through our website.\n\nIf you purchase a subscription from our website and are, for any reason, not happy with our service in the first 60 days, please email our support team at help@plantoeat.com, and we'll be happy to issue you a refund.\n\nRefunds should appear in your bank account approximately 5 business days after we acknowledge and process your refund request. \n\n### Refunds for purchases in the Apple App Store:\n\nIf you purchased our app from the App Store, you will need to send your refund request directly to Apple. Apple doesn't allow us to issue a refund for in-app purchases because we do not own them.\n\nHere's how to send your request:\n\n  1. Go to https://reportaproblem.apple.com\n\n  2. Log in with your Apple ID and password.\n\n  3. View your purchased apps. \n\n  4. Click on Report a Problem next to your Plan to Eat purchase.\n\n  5. You will be prompted to choose a reason for your refund request. Be sure to specifically describe your problem in the comment box. \n\n  6. Submit it to Apple.\n\nGenerally, all sales are final in the App Store, but Apple gives refunds on a case-by-case, exception basis. If the refund is denied, we recommend you contact Apple support and see if you can get more information or a refund appeal. "
